  "id": "DrugBank_DB06185 - MONDO_15812",
  "verbalization": "Forodesine shows a strong association with Primary Cutaneous Gamma/delta-positive T-cell Lymphoma, as evidenced by its indication in two distinct but related lymphoma subtypes. Path_5765 and Path_5766 both link Forodesine to Aggressive Primary Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma, which in turn is classified as Primary Cutaneous Gamma/delta-positive T-cell Lymphoma. Path_5767 further strengthens this relationship by showing Forodesine's indication in Primary Cutaneous Aggressive Epidermotropic Cd8+ T-cell Lymphoma, which also leads to the same final diagnosis. The shared pathway from Forodesine to the target lymphoma suggests a potential mechanism involving T-cell activation or proliferation, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a mechanistic link, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific biological pathway.",
